    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0131" n="71" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg71"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Marsh.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 189.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 28, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Recurring to your dispatch of the 6th of
                    February, No. 204, I have to inform you that, a free conversation has been had
                    between Mr. Cerruti and myself, in regard to the departure of an Italian fleet
                    to the waters of the La Plata. Probably I shall instruct Mr. Asboth to use his
                    good offices with discretion, for a pacific and friendly adjustment between
                    Italy and the republic of Paraguay.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">George P. Marsh</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
